// topology — canonical checked-boundary topology package
// (TASKS.md TOPOLOGY-PLAN-VERIFICATION; contract:
// wiki/spec/packages/topology.md).
//
// The package owns the v1 wire tables, graph normalization, the fixed
// `no_route`/`only_via` predicates, plan composition, and the independent
// source-free plan verification — an ordinary package with no compiler
// privilege. The Omega realization reuses the Rust reference's semantics
// (omega-rust/omega/packages/topology): same canonical byte layout (LE
// integers, u32 length prefixes, canonical-order rosters, the v1 tag
// table) and the same verification order — decode, request commitment,
// roster exactness, per-instance component binding, transport membership,
// then independent predicate replay against the recorded certificates.
//
// Input confinement: the verifier consumes only caller-staged bytes —
// `plan`, `request`, and per-instance verified `description` byte buffers
// staged through `feed_*`/`open_*` machines. No plan-declared claim is
// trusted: `verify` replays every required predicate itself and checks
// each recorded certificate against the reconstructed edge set, so a
// stored success flag, a stale request, a substituted component record,
// and an unselected verifier identity all reject by comparison or replay
// — never by loading code.
//
// Bounds: this realization fixes the v1 roster scale at
// MAX_INSTANCES=8, MAX_ENDPOINTS_PER_INSTANCE=8, MAX_BINDINGS=16,
// MAX_POLICIES=8, MAX_SELECTOR_MEMBERS=8, MAX_ASSUMPTIONS_PER_INSTANCE=4,
// MAX_ACCEPTED=32, MAX_TRANSPORTS=8 — an unsuccessful verification, never
// a satisfied verdict, on exhaustion. The Rust reference's larger limits
// (MAX_INSTANCES=1024 et al.) are the wire contract; a wider realization
// moves to dynamically-sized carriers when the language admits them.
//
// Stage status: `digest` + `verify` are implemented — the request,
// plan, and components decoders plus the full check pipeline
// (commitment, roster, component binding, assumptions, bindings/graph
// normalization, policy coverage + verifier identity, and independent
// no_route/only_via predicate replay with certificate closure checks
// over the reconstructed adjacency).
use digest;
use verify;
